From: ScarlettMac <scarlettmac@local>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:41:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/15] shader: run LDS flag regions on 32-lane GPUs (port of
 Belobug PR #4)

11 of upstream bf99e72's remaining 58 refusals are 'LDS one console
wave64 shares without barriers' (runs/20261126-152702-up720.log). When the
divergent LDS region only raises a flag, a read that misses the other host
wave's write changes nothing it leaves behind: every access is a
ds_read_b32/ds_write_b32 at a constant address, every write stores the same
constant, only one address is both read and written, the region has no
other effect, and no register it writes is live where a lane leaves it.
Such regions now run in host waves of 32 without a barrier.

Adapted from Belobug/VIctory-Belobug-AMD a5e42338 (PR #4) to upstream's
emit/lower/halves.rs and lower/barriers.rs: the region check uses
branch_regions, and split_wave_barriers gained an allowing form keyed on
the flag blocks. Other divergent LDS stays refused.

Test (host): the flag program lowers in waves of 32; a second, different
value written after the read is still refused.
